{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785702263,"nonce":"IwfzXEf6STO8f8bK8FK+qLeJEEE=","title":"Decided 2026-08-03 (grill; ADR-0066). ~10k lines across `export.rs`, `farm.rs`, `changeset.rs` and the Export half of `settle.rs`, whose only purpose was lazy delivery — cancelled on measurement (git-bug `4ce7f2c`). Verified there is **no control-plane or executor caller**: an HTTP-route grep for `v1/exports` matches only `workspaced.rs`, and an HTTP caller must contain the path literal, so this cannot be a trait-object-dispatch false negative.","message":"**Why delete rather than keep dormant.** Dormant is not free: live HTTP routes are attack surface (we Browse-gated `/v1/exports*` last week precisely because any fence token could DELETE another fence's Export), every refactor pays to keep it compiling (the ledger work already had to reason about it), and it invites someone to wire it up without re-reading why it was shelved. It stays in git, and ADR-0066 records what it was.\n\n**Three carve-outs — do not delete these:**\n- [ ] **EXTRACT THE FENCE-RESIDUE SWEEP FIRST** out of `sweep_exports_once` — the ledger and drain-record TTLs live inside it and are load-bearing for the HA design\n- [ ] **KEEP `changeset.rs` and its test tier** (`just overlay-tests-colima`) — the only code anywhere that reads an overlayfs upper, finally executed 2026-08-02 (git-bug `0ad393c`), and exactly what a revived laziness effort would want intact\n- [ ] **KEEP the reflink primitive** (now `reflink-copy`) — a future node-local cache wants it\n- [ ] Then remove the Export routes, the registry, the Farm, and the Export half of settle\n- [ ] ADR-0062 amended to name the revival path: **JuiceFS + its CSI driver, not a rebuild**","files":null}]}